# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is the public-facing repository. `code/` and `formalisation/` are the
# only directories it tracks. Everything else in the working tree is private
# working material and is listed here.
#
#   paper/               the manuscript (v1, v2, fragments, series). It is its
#                        own local-only git repository; nothing in it is ever
#                        pushed anywhere.
#   literature/          third-party papers. Copyright is not ours to publish.
#   project_management/  task boards, review notes, WRITING_STYLE.md, STATE.txt.
#   CLAUDE.md            working rules for this checkout.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/paper/
/literature/
/project_management/
/CLAUDE.md

# Retired computations, kept on disk because they may be useful to a later
# project, but not part of this paper and not published with it:
#   legacy/magma/  the pi-descent written for the withdrawn Paper I
#   legacy/sage/   the six-prime "A5 certificate" pipeline, the reach
#                  measurement, and the table generators that fed it
#   legacy/gp/     superseded one-off gp scripts
#   legacy/data/   the raw output of every run above
/code/legacy/

# Retired Lean declarations, kept on disk for the record but outside Lake's
# build and outside scripts/audit.sh:
#   legacy/Anchors.lean  the withdrawn anchor corollaries cor_sha5/cor_sha13,
#                        the Certificates structure and its two Fact instances,
#                        and the digit-certificate extraction lemmas
/formalisation/legacy/

# Belt and braces. The manuscript must never be committed here, whatever
# directory it is copied into.
main.tex
main.pdf
STATE.txt

# Staged output of an interrupted or failed run of a script under code/gp or
# code/sage. A clean run moves the file onto code/data/ and leaves nothing behind.
/code/data/*.partial

.DS_Store
.claude/
